 points?\n136|Fushiguro|I wonder why he added this rule.\n137|Yuji|He\'s killed 40 people at the very least, right?\n138|Yuji|I doubt he has nice intentions.\n139|Fushiguro|Still, this means we might be able to progress \\Nthrough the Culling Game without killing anyone.\n140|Fushiguro|Kogane, can you show a list of players \\Nwith 100 points or more?\n141|Kogane|Well, I\'m assigned to Itadori Yuji, so...\n142|Yuji|Oh, it\'s fine.\n143|Yuji|Go ahead and do what he asked.\n144|Fushiguro|People like Tsumiki who got caught up in this \\Nmay not engage unless they\'re desperate to escape.\n145|Fushiguro|The incarnated sorcerers must have had \\Ntheir own reasons for contracting with Kenjaku.\n146|Fushiguro|None of them are especially motivated to add rules.\n147|Fushiguro|If there\'s anyone else like Kashimo \\Nsitting on an excess of points...\n148|Yuji|Oh, I get it!\n149|Yuji|We find someone with 100 points or more \\Nwho has no interest in adding rules...\n150|Fushiguro|...and make them add a rule \\Nto let Tsumiki escape the Culling Game!\n151|Kogane|Here you are.\n152|Fushiguro|There\'s another one!\n153|Both|Yeah!\n154|Fushiguro|The first thing we need to do \\Nis deal with Rule 8.\n155|Yuji|Huh?\n156|Panda|What was Rule 8 again?\n157|Fushiguro|{\\blur1\\c&H000000&}It\'s the one that says if your points \\Ndon\'t change within nineteen days,\n158|Fushiguro|It\'s the one that says if your points \\Ndon\'t change within nineteen days,\n159|Fushiguro|your technique gets stripped, \\Nleading to death.\n160|Fushiguro|To counter that, we add a rule saying, \\N"Players can transfer points to each other."\n161|Fushiguro|Then we can keep passing points \\Namong ourselves\n162|Fushiguro|and avoid dying from \\Nhaving our techniques stripped.\n163|Fushiguro|If possible, we add one more.\n164|Fushiguro|A rule that says, \\N"Players may expend points to leave the Culling Game."\n165|Hakari|Wouldn\'t that conflict with the continuation clause? {when did hakari learn about the rules? did he watch that summary video they made?}\n166|Fushiguro|Yeah, I think it would.\n167|Fushiguro|But if we add a condition like dragging a non-player \\Ninto the Culling Game as a substitute, it might work.\n168|Hakari|True.\n169|Hakari|Would Kogane be making the call on that?\n170|Yuji|Either way, we know what we need to do now.\n171|Fushiguro|Yeah.\n172|Fushiguro|While searching for the Angel \\Nto break the seal on the Prison Realm,\n173|Fushiguro|we\'ll go after Kashimo Hajime and Higuruma Hiromi\n174|Fushiguro|and hunt them down.\n175|Yuji|Yeah, there\'s no "Angel" on here.\n176|Panda|That probably isn\'t her real name, \\Njust like you and Sukuna. {oda level foreshadowing} {CR: Just like you\'re not listed as Sukuna.}\n177|Fushiguro|{*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} said she was in eastern Tokyo.\n178|Fushiguro|That would be Colony No. 2, then.\n179|Hakari|You guys know what she looks like?']' timed out after 60 seconds
